
"smart_sources:2026-05-11 - Gas Tax Holiday Wouldn’t Help Drivers, But Would Hurt U.S. Highways.md": {"path":"2026-05-11 - Gas Tax Holiday Wouldn’t Help Drivers, But Would Hurt U.S. Highways.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1dbar6x","at":1785795032680},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1783543833167,"size":4389,"at":1785795032776,"hash":"1dbar6x"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,29]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Thomas Aiello","target":"Thomas Aiello","line":5}],"metadata":{"title":"Gas Tax Holiday Wouldn’t Help Drivers, But Would Hurt U.S. Highways","source":"https://www.ntu.org/publications/detail/open-letter-to-congress-suspension-of-federal-gas-tax-is-not-the-answer","author":["[[Thomas Aiello]]"],"published":"2026-05-11","created":"2026-07-08","description":"May 12, 2026  Open Letter to Congress: Suspension of Federal Gas Tax Is Not the Answer  As you consider policy responses to rising energy costs, National Taxpayers Union (NTU) cautions against a temporary suspension of the federal gasoline and diesel tax. While such proposals may appear politically appealing in the short term, they would do little to provide meaningful relief to consumers while creating significant long-term fiscal and infrastructure challenges. Congress should instead pursue po May 12, 2026  Dear Member of Congress,  As you consider policy responses to rising energy costs, National Taxpayers Union (NTU) cautions against a temporary suspension of the federal gasoline and diesel tax. While such proposals may appear politically appealing in the short term, they would do little to provide meaningful relief to consumers while creating significant long-term fiscal and infrastructure challenges. Congress should instead pursue policies that address the root causes of high ener, Author(s): Thomas Aiello"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},